  "text": "umably, the answer would be 10, as the powers of 3 up to \\(3^3=27\\) would be needed to sum up to 2010.\n\nTo find the least possible sum of the exponents, we would need to consider the powers of 3 that add up to 2010. This involves a bit of trial and error, but we can start by finding the largest power of 3 that is less than or equal to 2010. The largest power of 3 that is less than 2010 is \\(3^6 = 729\\). Subtracting 729 from 2010 gives us 1281. We continue this process until we have subtracted all the powers of 3 from 2010. The least possible sum of the exponents is the sum of the exponents of the powers of 3 that we subtract from 2010. In this case, the least possible sum of the exponents is 10, as we would need to subtract \\(3^6, 3^5, 3^4, 3^3, 3^2, 3^1, 3^0\\) from 2010 to get to 0.",
